<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Suluk</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 738</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a> · Also known as Abu Muzahim</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Suluk was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khagan">khagan</a> of the Turgesh, a Turkic people of the Western Tien Shan, from about 716 until 738. Allied with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibetans">Tibetans</a> and Sogdian princes, he fought the Umayyad <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabs">Arabs</a> for control of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transoxiana">Transoxiana</a>, defeating them on the 'Day of Thirst' in 724 and inflicting heavy losses at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-defile">Battle of the Defile</a> in 731. The Arabs nicknamed him Abu Muzahim, 'the one who jostles'. After a defeat at Kharistan he was murdered in 738.</p></div>
